title: 'pallet-xcm: migrate from LockableCurrency to fungible freezes'

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |
    Migrates `pallet-xcm` off the deprecated `Currency`/`LockableCurrency` traits onto the
    `fungible` trait family. Assets locked locally for a remote unlocker (`LockAsset` /
    `UnlockAsset`) are now held by a `fungible` freeze under `FreezeReason::AssetLock` instead of
    the `py/xcmlk` balance lock. Part of #7226 / #226.

    Config changes (breaking):
    - `Currency: LockableCurrency<AccountId, Moment = BlockNumberFor<Self>>` is replaced by
      `Currency: fungible::{Inspect, MutateFreeze}` with `Id = Self::RuntimeFreezeReason`.
    - `RuntimeFreezeReason` is added and must be set to the runtime's overarching freeze reason.
    - `OldCurrency: InspectLockableCurrency` is added, kept solely so the legacy `py/xcmlk` lock
      can be released while migrating. It can be removed once all locks have been converted.

    Runtimes configuring `pallet-xcm` therefore also need `pallet-balances` (or whichever fungible
    they use) to expose the overarching freeze reason: `FreezeIdentifier = RuntimeFreezeReason` and
    a `MaxFreezes` that covers its variant count. The in-tree runtimes that had freezes disabled
    (`FreezeIdentifier = ()`, `MaxFreezes = ConstU32<0>`) have been updated accordingly. This is a
    type-level change only for chains whose `CurrencyMatcher` matches nothing, since those can
    never create an XCM lock in the first place.

    Migration:
    - `pallet_xcm::migration::MigrateLocksToFreezes` is a multi-block migration (`SteppedMigration`)
      that walks `LockedFungibles` and converts each account's legacy lock into the equivalent
      freeze. It is registered in the Rococo and Westend relay chain runtimes, the only in-tree
      runtimes with existing state whose `CurrencyMatcher` can match an asset, and therefore the
      only ones that can hold a legacy lock. `LockedFungibles` itself is unchanged, so there is no
      storage version bump.
    - Accounts are additionally migrated lazily: locking or unlocking again releases any legacy
      lock once the equivalent freeze is in place. Chains that cannot host a multi-block migration
      rely on this path.

    Out of scope: `pallet-xcm` still supports a single fungible only. Moving to `fungibles` is
    deliberately left to a follow-up, because `LockedFungibles` stores no asset id and so multiple
    currencies require a new storage layout plus a second state migration on top of this one.

    Behaviour changes:
    - `prepare_lock` now also fails with `LockError::NoResources` when the account cannot take
      another freeze, so that `enact` cannot fail after the lock has been accounted for.
    - Fully unlocking an account now removes the restriction entirely, where the old code left a
      zero-amount `py/xcmlk` lock behind.
    - `try_state` gained an invariant checking that every `LockedFungibles` entry is backed by an
      equivalent freeze, or by the legacy lock if the account has not been migrated yet.

